// A minimal genuine cycle with no base case anywhere — `permission x`'s
// only rewrite rule is its own self-reference via `parent`, with no
// direct grant to fall back to. Deliberately pathological, for the CHC
// tier's own HOLDS-direction unit test (`test/chc.test.ts`,
// docs/DECISIONS.md, the entry adding `src/smt/chc.ts`): the least
// fixpoint of a relation nothing ever grounds is empty, for every object
// — a real, unconditional proof that recursion alone can decide, with
// genuine cycle termination (not "up to k", not "up to depth d").
//
// This exact shape is *also* already decided directly by `checkInvariant`
// (§5's own exact monotone search, cycle-safe since D-129) — no
// intersection/exclusion anywhere reachable from the goal — so
// `checkAndValidate` never actually routes it to this new tier; this
// fixture's own tests call `tryChcTier` directly instead, the same way
// `test/smt.test.ts` unit-tests the non-recursive tier's own encoder in
// isolation rather than only through the full router.
namespace folderx {
  relation parent: folderx
  permission x = parent->x
}
